{
  "abstract": "The full original run-count law has optimal quadratic Poisson–Charlier error with exact mean and second factorial cumulant, a uniform mean-bias bound and eventual probability status. Exact and nominal Poisson total variation have their distinct remainder powers and the same moving residue equivalent. Every fixed polynomial weight and factorial moment, the zero-count probability, and the literal integer quantization and cost of replacing the exact mean are recorded.",
